# PREDICTION for ROOT lane run 18, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run.
#
# STEP -1 of `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md`. The derivation is written out so it is
# checkable independently of whether the number matches. R19-06, R20-07 and D0A-R26-06 are
# three runs whose FIGURE was right and whose EXPLANATION was wrong — the last in this file.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION, NOT MECHANISM (D0A-R22-01, reopened). Held for runs 13-17.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THIS RUN'S PREDICTION IS THE SAME NUMBER AS RUN 17'S MEASUREMENT. READ THAT CAREFULLY.
# =========================================================================================
#
#   EXPECTED 208 / 5 / 213   — IDENTICAL to run 17's measured 208 / 5 / 213.
#
# **So the count check has nothing to detect this round, and a matching number is nearly
# uninformative.** The round-29 remediation changed CODE and added no tests: R29-04 RENAMED a
# test rather than adding one, and R29-05, R29-06 and R29-08 are code fixes with no tests at
# all. A green 208 therefore says the suite still passes on changed code — which is worth
# having — and says nothing whatever about whether the changed code is covered.
#
# THE MEMBERSHIP CHECK HAS EXACTLY ONE THING TO SEE, and it is nameable in advance. Measured
# by diffing `--list` at HEAD against run 17's log (both 213 identities):
#
#   in HEAD, not run 17:  wire::tests::read_frame_applies_no_deadline_to_a_cooperating_peer
#   in run 17, not HEAD:  wire::tests::read_frame_does_not_bound_a_wait_on_a_cooperating_peer
#
# One rename, both directions, nothing else. **Within run 18 itself** the root log and the
# unprivileged `--list` are taken from the same tree, so §4b must show 213 each side and ZERO
# in either direction; the rename is a CROSS-RUN observation, recorded here so it is not
# mistaken for a within-run mismatch.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY RUN 18 IS OWED: THE CODE MOVED EVEN THOUGH THE COUNT DID NOT
#
#   * R29-04 — `read_frame` now takes its deadline from `client_deadline_policy()`. The
#     production wrapper changed shape.
#   * R29-05 — the daemon's exit path now tracks per-child terminal state, keeps the guard
#     ARMED on cleanup failure, and RETURNS AN ERROR instead of success. **This changes what
#     `delphi-runtimed` does on exit**, at root, where children are real.
#   * R29-06 — `ChildGuard::reap_status` retries EINTR and disarms only after a terminal
#     status. It guards forked children in root tests; its failure mode was a HUNG HARNESS.
#   * R29-08 — `check-free-space.sh` now resolves cargo's target dir via `cargo metadata`.
#     §0 of the procedure exercises it directly.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN RUN 18 WILL NOT ESTABLISH — stated BEFORE the run, because a green at 208 will
# otherwise read as covering these. That over-read is exactly what the `b1_daemon_binary` skip
# produced last round, and it is being pre-empted rather than corrected afterwards.
#
# 1. **R29-05 AND R29-06 SHIPPED WITHOUT TESTS OF THEIR OWN.** Recorded as owed, not counted.
#    - R29-05's new path (a child unreaped after SIGKILL → guard stays armed → daemon returns
#      an error) requires a child in uninterruptible sleep. **Nothing constructs one.**
#    - R29-06's new path (EINTR during `waitpid` → retry) requires a signal delivered inside
#      the wait window. **Nothing delivers one.** The reviewer reproduced it with a
#      signal-injection probe; that probe is theirs, not in this tree.
#    So both fixes will be *compiled and linked* by run 18 and *exercised* by nothing.
#
# 2. **R28-02'S COVERAGE GAP IS OPEN FOR A SECOND CONSECUTIVE ROUND.** The bounded daemon exit
#    is still the most root-relevant change in the arc and still unexercised at root:
#    `b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow` SKIPS here for want of
#    `--features insecure-test-seams`, and even unskipped `delphi-minimal-ai` cooperates, so
#    the SIGKILL branch is never taken. R29-05 has now MODIFIED that same untested path.
#    **A change to untested code does not become tested by being changed.**
#    The reviewer's answer, owed: extract the exit sequence so `main` calls the EXTRACTED
#    implementation rather than a duplicate, covering a cooperating child (status preserved),
#    a child synchronised past grace expiry, interrupted waits, signalling failure, post-kill
#    reap timeout, already-reaped children, and each child independently — then assembly
#    coverage that the daemon invokes the policy after terminal outcomes.
#
# 3. THE MUTATION CAMPAIGN IS UNPRIVILEGED-ONLY (`euid=1000`). Nothing in a lane run is a
#    campaign. The five root-gated tests have never been mutation-tested.
#
# 4. THE SUSPEND DIVERGENCE is unmeasured; the clock test prints its own delta and says so.
#
# 5. `action.timeout` IS ENFORCED NOWHERE (R9-04); round 28 closed its digest binding only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVATION
#
# Base: run 17 measured EXECUTED 208 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 213, membership proven by identity.
#       Current unprivileged pair: EXECUTED 188 / SKIPPED 25 / reported 213 (measured
#       2026-09-07 at 93124b0, re-measured by the pre-commit hook across all 17 targets).
#
# Delta since run 17: **ZERO tests added or removed**; one rename (above). No test changed its
# root-gating: no `geteuid` check, `SKIP` branch or `bwrap_available` guard was added or
# removed by the round-29 remediation — verified by grepping the diff for those tokens.
#
# So: 208 EXECUTED, skip set unchanged at 5, reported 213.
#   unprivileged  188 + 25 = 213
#   root          208 +  5 = 213
# Equal totals are NOT the evidence (D0A-R27-04); §4b's identity comparison is.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TIMING TOLERANCES — carried forward, and one is now WEAKER on purpose
#
#   read_frame_applies_no_deadline_...  its load-bearing assertion is now on the POLICY
#                                       (`client_deadline_policy().is_none()`), which has NO
#                                       timing dependence at all. Its 900 ms behavioural half
#                                       remains and is the only part load can affect —
#                                       deliberately, because D0A-R29-04 found that a timing
#                                       assertion could only catch bounds shorter than its own
#                                       sleep, and the real one was 30 s.
#   a_frame_whose_last_byte_...         80 ms deadline, final byte ~150 ms; asserts REFUSAL
#   a_stalled_ / a_trickling_           400 ms absolute deadline, `elapsed < 5 s`
#   boot_secs_agrees_...                1 s sampling gap
#
# The stall/trickle pair still fail in opposite directions under load, so a slow machine cannot
# make both pass by accident.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A MISMATCH IS A RESULT. Record which side was wrong. Do not adjust this derivation until it
# agrees with the measurement.

EXPECTED_EXECUTED=208
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
EXPECTED_REPORTED=213
